From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:58:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] guest: verify sealed mounts and native initdata binding

Before forwarding container creation to the guest agent, match
sealed-volume descriptors to the measured manifest and unseal their
contents through CDH into private mounts. Reject plaintext substitution
and attempts by other containers to mount the private secret tree.

Bind exact initdata through the native AA ttrpc API and verify one
canonical SHA-384 TCG2 event. Reject disabled measurement, mismatched
digests and duplicate extension. In the measured ephemeral profile,
reject injected cloud volumes before device preparation.

Delay CDH connection until descriptor validation. Use one container-create
transaction to roll back all newly acquired resources on every failure and
retain ownership when cleanup must be retried. Delegate CopyFile confinement
to the pinned Kata agent shared-root implementation.

